WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.270
Look at your Mobile phone for a second.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:07.950
If you opened it up, you would see something
similar to this…

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.959
…lots of microchips, small semiconductors
and circuits.

00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:16.619
In order to manufacture all of this, you need
a very special element: TANTALUM.

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:18.440
Where does this tantalum come from?

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.789
Well, mainly from one country: the Democratic
Republic of CONGO.

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:26.720
One of the World’s poorest countries.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.699
It’s impossible to estimate how many people
have died in order to manufacture the phone

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:38.550
you have in your hands right now.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.629
Tantalum is one of the most highly demanded
materials on the planet.

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:43.820
And Congo has the largest reserves.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.400
It could be an enormous source of wealth to
them.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.780
A country that also has lots of natural resources.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.949
Nonetheless, Congo is one of the poorest and
most violent countries on Earth.

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:58.530
And believe me, their history is much more
complex than those clickbait articles you’ve

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.810
found on your twitter feed.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.879
So why is Congo so poor?

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:13.110
In this video, we’ll tell you the story.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.590
Congo was featured in that movie ‘Gorillas
in the mist’.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.810
It’s funny, because we don’t know anything
about this country, despite how often pop

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.280
culture references it…

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.090
We’re talking about one of the biggest countries
on the planet.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:33.780
It has more than 80 million inhabitants living
within a territory the size of Western Europe.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.780
And oh boy!

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:39.500
They have a hell of a fortune under their
feet: cobalt, gold and, of course, COLTAN.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.350
Coltan is the ore that tantalum is taken from.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:51.780
So we all have products imported from Congo
in our home.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.430
Many of you might say: wow!

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.630
They’re so lucky, having so many natural
resources, right?

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.360
In fact, the opposite is true.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:05.909
All this gold, cobalt and, especially, coltan,
is actually a curse for Congo.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:09.570
Yes, my dear viewers, Congo is one of the
poorest countries on the planet.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:13.560
And we’re talking about so called absolute
poverty here.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:21.290
Most of the population lives on less than
a dollar

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:22.290
a day.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.290
Starvation is common.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.860
And guerrilla warfare is so typical in this
country that it’s no longer newsworthy.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.570
But you already know this.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.830
The question is…

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:31.830
Why?

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.560
And the answer is a combination of all the
bad things we usually mention here on VisualPolitik:

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.960
wars, bad governance, corruption and, of course,
colonialism.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.670
Imagine all of this on a massive scale and
you have a good high level picture of Congo.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.670
So…

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:47.680
OK!

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.690
Done!

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.570
We already know why Congo is so poor.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.480
End of the story… right?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.230
Oh come on!

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.980
This is VisualPolitik.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.570
The case of Congo is unique in history.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:06.670
We can’t even compare it with other African
nations.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:12.310
So, if you know VisualPolitik, you already
know that we’re going to cover all the details

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.920
about this country.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.510
Including the result of their latest elections.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.120
So the question here is…

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.030
Why is Congo so poor?

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.590
Why do we say that their natural resources
are a curse?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.940
And… the most important question of all…

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.160
Can their brand new president lift this curse?

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.200
Today we’re going to answer all of these
questions but, before we do, let’s take

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.960
a look back at the history.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.980
HOW TO PRIVATIZE A COUNTRY

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.350
In the year 1877, king Leopold II of Belgium
bought Congo.

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:46.070
Yes, you heard that right.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:50.210
Usually, when we talk about colonization,
we mean a country conquering another one,

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.210
right?

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.770
Well, so here’s the first unique thing about
this story.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:59.090
What we know today as Congo was a land with
many tribes, and a land with a huge potential

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.090
to grow rubber.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.850
In a time when pneumatics were being produced
on a mass scale, rubber was in high demand.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:08.130
King Leopold II looked at this opportunity
with dollar signs in his eyes and said: why

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.720
conquer a country if you can buy it?

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:19.739
You see, it was a different time and, back
then, European powers thought they could do

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:21.260
anything they wanted in Africa.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.700
On one hand, it was a source of wealth to
be exploited.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.870
On the other, they thought colonization was
a matter of charity.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:33.320
They wanted to export European values and
civilization to a ‘land of barbarity’.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:38.540
This is why Leopold II created the International
African Association, an organization led by

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:48.150
him that allowed him to go to Congo and create
his own factories and plantations.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:52.400
Since the Congolese people had no private
property, Leopold II could take over the land

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.460
without any kind of contract.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:59.090
Of course, in order to legitimize this looting,
Leopold II, the king of a respectable country

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:08.440
like Belgium, claimed he would turn this ‘Free
State of Congo’ into a civilized place.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.220
The Congo Free State is unique in its kind.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:16.700
It has nothing to hide and no secrets and
is not beholden to anyone except its founder.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.870
–Leopold II, King of Belgium

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.370
The reality was way different.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.430
Leopold II wanted to get as much rubber as
possible.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.840
So he enslaved the population and forced them
to reach production quotas.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.640
If they didn’t, he would chop off one of
their hands.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:35.990
This is how one of the worst genocides in
history started.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:40.370
Something comparable, in relative terms, to
Mao’s cultural revolution.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:45.190
The massacre was so terrible even other colonial
powers such as the United Kingdom denounced

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:52.280
Leopold for his atrocities.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:56.060
If you wanna know more about this, I have
a video about King Leopold II on my other

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.000
channel, Biographix.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.340
But let’s move on with today’s story.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.210
After Leopold II died, he passed his property
over to the state of Belgium.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.220
This is how Congo became a colony in its own
right.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.639
Belgium’s government was a little more compassionate
than the king but, still, the Congolese were

00:06:12.639 --> 00:06:14.420
kept in slave-like conditions.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.660
You see, colonialism is one of the most despicable
practices in history.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.710
But if there is one colonial power that was
big on brutality, it’s Belgium.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:28.080
And if you want to be even more angry, let
me tell you that to this day, there are lots

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:34.900
of monuments, buildings and streets in Brussels
dedicated to Leopold II.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:40.770
But the truth is, in 1960, Congo got its independence.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.100
This doesn’t mean things got better for
them.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:47.330
Their first president, PATRICE LUMUMBA, was
no big fan of his former colonizers.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:52.080
This is why both France and Belgium helped
other groups to overthrow and execute him.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.990
Which is how MOBUTU SESE SEKO’s dictatorship
started and the country changed its name to

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:57.990
ZAIRE.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.610
Mobutu is known as one of the bloodiest dictators
in history.

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:06.889
But, as we often say at VisualPolitik, Mobutu
may have been a son of a bitch, but he was

00:07:06.889 --> 00:07:09.320
OUR son of bitch.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:15.680
You know, it was the cold war, and Congo was
an ally of the West.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.200
So there was always money to finance his army.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.610
But things changed in the 90s.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.669
Without a USSR to be afraid of, America stopped
supporting Mobutu.

00:07:23.669 --> 00:07:27.010
And all those groups he was oppressing rebelled
against him.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:31.180
This is how the first Congolese civil war
started… and the country got back its current

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.180
name.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.360
A civil war that led to another second civil
war.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:38.840
For a better understanding of just how devastating
this conflict was, the Second Congolese civil

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:44.400
war is considered to be the deadliest conflict
after World War II, with over 5 million deaths

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.350
and countless acts of torture, mutilation,
and other atrocities.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.020
But…

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.520
Here’s the worst thing.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.419
The violence has not stopped.

00:07:55.419 --> 00:07:57.230
In 2003, the war ended.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:00.860
Since then, Joseph KABILA has tried to be
a dictator who rules over the country with

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.860
an iron fist.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:02.860
But, let’s be honest.

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:06.389
As authoritarian and corrupted as he is, he
can’t control the country.

00:08:06.389 --> 00:08:09.050
There are guerrillas and looting from neighbouring
countries all the time.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.389
And you might wonder…

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.670
Why is there so much guerrilla warfare?

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.050
How can one country have so many armed groups?

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.980
How do they pay for those guns?

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:23.710
Let’s have a look, shall we?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.710
COLTAN RUSH

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.919
Do you remember the NOKIA 6110?

00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:30.740
This phone was launched at the end of the
90s and was one of the first cell phones to

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:37.140
reach a massive audience.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:44.190
Suddenly, everybody had a mobile phone.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.380
And this meant more and more tantalum was
required to produce those.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:51.050
Until that moment, the main tantalum producer
was Australia.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.200
The problem?

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.560
Getting that material was more expensive than
you might imagine.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:09:03.240
You see… it’s almost impossible to find
pure chemical elements in nature.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:08.830
In this case, Australia had mines where you
could find some ore and, after a complex chemical

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.960
process, get a little bit of tantalum out
of it.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.010
But there is an easier way to obtain it.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:15.390
Yes, my dear viewers, I’m talking about
COLTAN.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:19.460
COLTAN is a rock that contains a lot of tantalum
and it’s very cheap to refine.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:23.050
And guess where you can find the biggest coltan
reserves on the planet?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.050
Exactly!

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:25.050
In Congo.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:29.940
Basically, Congo is the Saudi Arabia of coltan.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:36.350
There’s plenty of it, it’s easy to extract
and easier to refine.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:40.620
In fact, you don’t even need technology
to get coltan: just a pick and shovel and…

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:41.630
there you go!

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:44.980
This is why thousands of Congolese joined
the coltan hunt.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.320
And, despite the high demand, tantalum became
cheaper and cheaper.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.080
But wait because this is just the beginning!

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.990
Remember the financial crisis of 2008?

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:58.450
Well, it also had some consequences in Australia.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:03.670
GAM closes Wodgina tantalum mine

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.640
This mine was the world’s main tantalum
producer.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.000
Its closure meant that tantalum prices skyrocketed.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.980
It’s hard to estimate the market price for
this material because, unlike oil, there are

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.300
no public indexes.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:19.000
But, according to some consultancy firms,
tantalum prices almost doubled from one year

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.000
to the next.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.100
And what was the consequence for Congo?

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.100
Exactly!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.540
A coltan rush!

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:28.860
All of a sudden, everybody was willing to
sacrifice their lives for a fistfull of rocks.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:29.860
Especially the warlords.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:34.480
This is how most of those guerrillas were
financed: by selling coltan.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.940
And the more tantalum they sold, the more
violent they became.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:46.480
We’re talking about such a huge massacre
that even America had to pass a law for it.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.670
Dodd-Frank Act Becomes Law

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:51.490
Basically, Dood Frank law was meant to protect
consumers.

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:54.560
One of its sections referred to so called
‘conflict minerals’.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.400
One of which was tantalum.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.650
According to this law, companies buying tantalum
should know where it comes from.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.650
The problem?

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:04.700
In a country like Congo, it’s almost impossible
to control the traceability of a mineral.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.240
Especially, given that there are almost no
mining companies.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:08.480
Yes, you heard that right.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.940
It’s mostly just common people going to
the countryside to extract rocks and sell

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.180
them to a man, who will sell them to another
man….

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:19.600
And finally, it ends up inside of your mobile
phone.

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:25.710
In many cases, Rwandan miners cross the border,
exploit the mines and then go back to Rwanda

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:26.710
to process it.

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:31.540
As you know, Rwanda is a country that’s
growing really fast and offers much more security,

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.300
in legal, political and physical terms, compared
to Congo.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.279
And… well, if you didn’t already know
this, here’s this other video we made a

00:11:37.279 --> 00:11:39.790
long time ago, telling that story.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:44.060
In fact, if you wanna know more about these
kinds of things, you should subscribe to VisualPolitik

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:46.120
and hit that bell button so you won’t miss
any posts.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.970
But let’s go back to our story.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.660
Many of you might wonder… since it’s so
profitable…

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:53.130
Why aren’t there any big mining companies?

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:57.430
Aren’t there incentives to create companies
that can mass produce coltan?

00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:59.100
The answer is NO.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.170
Why?

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:04.450
Well, here’s an example!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:09.120
Biggest Congo coltan miner resumes buying
after output halt

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.710
In this case, BISUNZU is one of the few Congolese
mining companies.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.050
It was founded by a Congolese senator that
wanted to industrialize mining.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:20.100
Instead of risking lives to get coltan, BISUNZU
wants to use machines.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.640
That way, they can offer better security for
the workers and extract a lot more minerals.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.540
So what’s their problem, then?

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.420
First, all of this machinery is expensive.

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:31.760
And Money is seldom abundant in Congo.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:35.430
Second, nobody would invest in a place where
corrupt politicians are going to make your

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.430
life impossible.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:43.480
And, if politicians don’t do it, then some
guerrilla will.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.450
So what happens then?

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:50.110
Nobody invests in this industry and those
who do, like BISUNZU, have to stop their production

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:53.240
all the time due to smugglers and warlords.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:57.490
And this is how we can understand the vicious
cycle of coltan.

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:01.290
The more demand there is, the more incentives
there are for warlords to exploit it.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:06.140
And the more warlords we have exploiting coltan,
the less incentives there are to create an

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:13.970
industry that would provide quality jobs and
create real wealth.

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:18.620
This is why, despite the fact that half of
the tantalum on the planet comes from this

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.160
area, Congo doesn’t grow any faster.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.110
And now you might wonder…

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.660
Can anybody change this?

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.700
Well… maybe… or maybe not.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:33.430
You’ll understand in a second.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:34.800
THE BIG FRAUD

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:35.970
Do you remember Joseph Kabila?

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:37.110
The Congolese dictator?

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:40.660
Well, in the year 2018, he had to resign and
call for elections.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:44.600
In fact, according to the Congolese constitution,
he should have done it before.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.110
But you know… dictators.

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:50.740
As you can imagine, 2018 couldn’t have been
more rigged.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:55.400
Kabila’s opponents only had one or two electoral
cabins.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:58.770
Citizens had to vote with tablets that nobody
knew how to use.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:05.870
And, well… no international observer accepted
this process…

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:10.490
Congo to EU: Mind your own business
An election that’s been delayed for two

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:15.240
years is about to be held, and the country
has booted out the EU ambassador.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:20.480
OK, so in this election, we had 3 main candidates:
RAMAZONI, who was Kabila’s successor, FAYULU,

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:24.580
his biggest opponent, and TSHISEKEDI, the
one with the lowest chance of winning.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:25.820
Guess who won!

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:26.820
Nope!

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:27.820
Not Ramazoni.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.530
The winner was TSHISEKEDI.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.540
And here’s where the debate starts.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.630
According to all the organizations observing
this process, including the catholic church,

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:41.209
the process couldn’t have been dirtier.

00:14:41.209 --> 00:14:44.040
Many analysts say that Kabila knew nobody
would accept his successor.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:46.370
So he let a moderate enemy win.

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.400
Somebody who, at least, would let Kabila keep
his fortune.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.899
Because make no mistake, despite Congo’s
poverty, Kabila is a millionaire.

00:14:52.899 --> 00:14:57.700
Then again, Donald Trump has supported TSHISEKEDI,
even if it’s only to guarantee some kind

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.300
of stable government for Congo.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:02.990
So now the question is… can this brand new
president change things?

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:08.220
Well… the truth is he does have opportunities.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:13.620
Lithium/tantalum: New Australian production
from Pilbara

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:17.550
Basically, the Australians have discovered
a brand new way to extract tantalum more cheaply.

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:19.050
So they’ve reopened their mine.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:20.769
What does this mean, then?

00:15:20.769 --> 00:15:25.450
Well… less of a coltan rush, less money
for the warlords and more incentives to create

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:27.589
an ethical and sustainable industry.

00:15:27.589 --> 00:15:31.361
On the other hand, Rwanda, Congo’s neighbouring
country, has been developing its own coltan

00:15:31.361 --> 00:15:32.420
processing industry.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.570
In 2018, they created a big factory to produce
tantalum.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:39.730
And they’re even experimenting with BLOCKCHAIN
technology to guarantee the traceability of

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.839
tantalum.

00:15:42.839 --> 00:15:46.120
This means it will now be easier to know where
our tantalum comes from.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:50.459
So now, this new Congolese government can
partner with Rwanda to create a coltan industry

00:15:50.459 --> 00:15:53.110
that generates jobs and growth.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:56.579
But here’s a question for you…

00:15:56.579 --> 00:15:59.850
Do you think the Congolese government will
be willing to do so?

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:04.550
Is this brand new president going to end the
rampant corruption in order to help his country

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:05.550
escape poverty?

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:10.310
Or… will we continue to see Congo as poor
as always despite its enormous natural wealth?

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.210
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:17.120
Before finishing, I’d like to thank SUZANE,
from ROSKILL, for helping us with the research.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:21.920
ROSKILL is one of the leading mining consultancy
companies and they were so kind to us, answering

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:26.610
our questions and giving us a lot of information
that is not easy to access.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:30.930
Also, don’t forget to visit our friends
from RECONSIDER MEDIA PODCAST, the podcast

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:34.820
that provided the voices on this episode that
were not mine and, as always, I’ll see you

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:45.769
next time.

